  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Let $m$ and $n$ be integers and let $q$ be a prime number. If $q∣mn,$ then{{field-1}}{{field-2}} $q∣n.$",
  "worked_solution": "For any integers $m$ and $n$ and any prime $q,$ we have that\n\n$$\nq∣mn\\,⟹\\,q∣m\\,\\text{or}\\,q∣n.\n$$",
